{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/Quadtree","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/ST"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A quadtree: elements at points in a rectangle, which finds those in a box, within a radius"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of a point, or nearest a point, and takes insertions and removals as the points move."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/spatialtrees\/quadtree"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Quadtree","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The rectangle is split into four equal quadrants, and each quadrant again, until every leaf"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"holds at most "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bucketCapacity"},{"type":"text","text":" elements (Finkel and Bentley, “Quad Trees: A Data Structure for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Retrieval on Composite Keys”, 1974). A search visits only the cells that meet its region."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Cells and elements live in flat arrays; a removal that leaves a cell’s quadrants holding no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"more than one bucket merges them back. Cells at depth 24 never split, so any number of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"elements may share one point."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["var map = Quadtree<String>(bounds: BoundingBox(lower: [0, 0], upper: [100, 100]))","map.insert(\"café\", at: [10, 20])","map.insert(\"library\", at: [12, 22])","map.insert(\"station\", at: [80, 75])","map.nearest(to: [11, 19])?.element                          \/\/ \"café\"","map.items(within: 5, of: [11, 21]).count                    \/\/ 2","map.items(in: BoundingBox(lower: [50, 50], upper: [100, 100])).map(\\.element)   \/\/ [\"station\"]"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A point on the line between two quadrants belongs to the upper one. The elements and their"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"points are a sequence, in no particular order."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees"]]},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"struct","modules":[{"name":"SpatialTrees"}],"title":"Quadtree","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Quadtree"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Quadtree"}],"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure","externalID":"s:12SpatialTrees8QuadtreeV","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/GrafluentCollections\/blob\/main\/Sources\/SpatialTrees\/Quadtree.swift#L24","fileName":"Quadtree.swift"}},"topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/Quadtree\/init(bounds:bucketCapacity:)"]},{"title":"Instance Properties","anchor":"Instance-Properties","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/Quadtree\/bounds","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/Quadtree\/bucketCapacity","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees